    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Flat epithelial atypia",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Monotonous cells with round nuclei are present in stratified layers that lack polarity. No architecture is formed (flat pattern), but the cells are similar to those seen in low-grade ductal carcinoma in&nbsp;situ and atypical ductal hyperplasia. ",
    "source": "Kimberly H. Allison",
    "copyright": "",
