    "chapterId": 9,
    "fileId": 51724,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Flat epithelial atypia",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Portions of two adjacent acini involved by a proliferation of atypical cuboidal epithelial cells with monotonous low-grade nuclei. The atypical cells form a monolayer in one acinus (top half of the image) and are stratified in two to four cell layers in the other acinus (lower half of the image). Both proliferations are flat, with no architectural complexity. ",
    "source": "Edi Brogi",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/84/9/51724.jpg",
