    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Columnar cell hyperplasia, CK5/6 staining pattern",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Columnar cell change characteristically has loss of CK5/6 staining, similarly to flat epithelial atypia; however, columnar cell hyperplasia may have CK5/6-staining cells proliferating at the tips of the epithelial projections as shown here. The underlying columnar cell change is CK5/6-negative.",
    "source": "Kimberly H. Allison",
